<title>USA: Sun to cut 200 jobs at Marcus Hook refinery.</title>
<headline>Sun to cut 200 jobs at Marcus Hook refinery.</headline>
<dateline>MARCUS HOOK, Pa. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Co on Wednesday said it will cut more than 200 jobs at its Marcus Hook, Pa., refinery as part of a competitive improvement plan in 1997.</p>
<p>Personnel cuts will come from contractors as well as the current 845 refinery jobs and will occur in both operations and maintenance, with a small number from other support areas. Output at the The 175,000-barrel-per-day refinery will not be reduced as a result of the personnel cutbacks, Sun said.</p>
<p>The plan is focused on improving reliability and reducing cash operating costs to a more competitive level through reductions in personnel, improved operating and maintenance procedures, and a reduction in energy costs, the firm said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610</p>
